{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3171-7658-9a46-3878c640b7e6","id":"01a1a592-1891-76a0-96d8-d41635564a0d","idempotency_key":"101df8c7d57484f240df3e2f1200733a9f3fea839dc159e887e6cc7501576a63","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T07:59:37Z","payload":{"note":"crates/ai/src/game.rs: MatchConfig/Player/MatchState/MatchMove/MatchResult/MatchSnapshot were already there; this adds the missing clocks and comments and puts the whole machine under test. Clocks: TimeControl {initial_ms, increment_ms} in MatchConfig (serde default, so existing stored configs and snapshots still load), ClockState per side with last_at, Match::tick(at) charging the side to move (first tick starts the clock, nothing is charged before it), Match::apply_at(input, at) charging then adding the increment, timeout result 1-0/0-1 with termination timeout and no move recorded, and a flagged match refusing further moves. The state machine stays pure: no wall clock is read, so a replay of the same moves at the same timestamps gives the same result. MatchSnapshot now carries the clock and the result, and from_snapshot restores both plus ply comments, which replaying moves alone cannot reproduce. PGN writes a TimeControl header when timed and a {comment} after an annotated ply, refusing a comment on a ply that was never played and neutralising a } that would break out of the braces. Server: create_match starts the clock at creation (previously the side to move thought for free until its first move), play_match_move charges via apply_at with the wall clock and returns bad_request on a flag, resign_match ticks first, and match_payload reports the clock. i-97b8 (persist transitions before side effects) holds trivially today: the route applies the move and saves the snapshot in one step and there is no broadcast to order against; when match events are streamed (t-1315/t-f26f) the save must move ahead of the emit. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features match -> 26 tests (every termination: checkmate, stalemate, insufficient material, max plies, resignation, timeout; move log with colours, SAN and UCI; custom start FEN; clock charging, increments, cumulative ticks, flagging; PGN headers, result, open matches and comments; snapshot replay with clock and comments; repository save and resume). Live: timed match 60s, 2s think, 57.98s left, resign charged the other side and ended 1-0 resignation.","target":"t-5364"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
